    heads this column "Noro Psychic / Promethean (First Stage)" and it is the
    O.C.C.''s table: 0 / 2,601 / 5,001 / 10,001 / 20,001 / 30,001 / 39,001 /
    52,001 / 70,001 / 100,001 / 140,001 / 190,001 / 240,001 / 290,001 /
    350,001, topping out at 520,000. frontmatter.md is explicit that a race
    carrying its own table wins over the occupation''s and silently drops it.
  - S.D.C. IS A BASE HERE, NOT A POOL BONUS. The line reads "1D6x100 S.D.C. and
    P.E.x5 hit points" with no "plus O.C.C. and skill bonuses" clause, so it is
    sdc_base rather than bonuses.pools.sdc - the opposite reading from the
    Pleasurer''s in #416, and it is the clause that decides, not the shape of the
    number. Because it is a base, this class needs no CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS entry.
    "M.D.C.: None, but see natural abilities" points at the phased body rather
    than at a pool, so there is no mdc_base either.
  - THE FOUR PHASE POWERS OR TEMPORAL SPELLS ARE NOT MODELLED. Up to four of the
    fourteen R.C.C. related picks may be spent on temporal magic spells or on
    phase powers instead of skills - "both can be learned, but they cannot total
    more than four, not four of each". A skill slot traded for a catalog entry
    of another kind is not a shape occ_related_skills has: its count is one open
    number over a category list. All fourteen are stored as skills and the trade
    is recorded here. The temporal magic half could not have been honoured in
    any case; see the Promethean Time Master.
  - Psionics: the four named powers are automatic to every promethean and are
    granted rather than picked. The three chosen at first level and the one per
    level after are gated to Healing, Sensitive and Physical, which is what the
    book says; Super is NOT opened here, and only the two phase O.C.C.s open it.
    "Considered a master psionic" is stored as the type.
  - THIS RACE''S PSIONICS DISPLACE THE PHASE ADEPT''S WHEN THE TWO ARE PLAYED
    TOGETHER. combineClasses in js/parser.js keeps whichever block is STRICTLY
    higher, and "Considered a master psionic" on printed 26 puts this race at
    the top of the ladder, so no O.C.C. block can ever beat it: the Phase
    Adept''s six phase powers, its super-psionic pick and its whole level
    schedule are discarded. Measured against the real parser rather than
    reasoned about. The Promethean Time Master is untouched, because it states
    no psionics of its own. Filed as BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F10, which also
    records the two noro O.C.C.s that have already shipped in this shape.
  - Equipment: the book gives no item list. It gives 2D6x10,000 credits in
    equipment or weapons PLUS 1D6x1000 credits in cash or trade items, so
    starting_money holds the cash figure only - starting money is coin, and an
    equipment allowance is not coin. Warrior-types favour segmented armor
    manufactured on Phase World (120 M.D.C.), optionally with a phase field at
    extra cost, and the race favours phase-tech weapons; neither is a specific
    item the gear catalog could name, so both are in the body instead.
  - Alignment: Any. Every promethean ready for the second stage is principled or
    scrupulous, but that is a condition of advancement rather than a restriction
    on the character, so no alignment is enforced.
