## Lore

First stage prometheans are large humanoids, seven to ten feet tall, with
barrel-shaped chests, thick limbs and round heads. Their grayish purple skin is
coarse, with the consistency and hardness of stone; their mouths are little more
than thin slits and their eyes are solid black beads. They have no noses and do
not need to breathe, drawing air through their mouths only to speak, and they
survive the vacuum of space unaided by any apparatus.

The "immature" prometheans are as intelligent as the adults of most sentient
races, roughly human-sized, and appear to have no genders as we understand them.
They know little about their second stage elders, and rather than trying to
understand what they will become they set out to learn as much as they can about
the rest of the universe. First stagers are found throughout the Three Galaxies
as pilots, explorers, travelers, tourists and adventurers, and a few as
smugglers and pirates. Their personalities run the whole human range, from dead
serious to clownish and from compassionate to vindictive - but prometheans treat
all of their own behaviour as part of a discovery process, so a formerly evil
promethean may see the error of his way and change completely. For that reason
they will almost never kill a member of their own race, however evil: in their
view there is always a chance of redemption.

Prometheans are the only race that has mastered phase technology and the only
sentient race that can step out of phase naturally, without it. They have one of
the highest I.Q. averages in the Three Galaxies, surpassed only by the
telepathic noro. They work closely with the draconids and are well regarded by
the Consortium of Civilized Worlds; the cosmo-knights respect them, though they
will not hesitate to stop a dangerous one. They are persecuted in the
Transgalactic Empire, and hated or feared across much of the Three Galaxies.

## Equipment and Wealth

The book states no item list. A first stage promethean begins with 2D6x10,000
credits'' worth of equipment or weapons of choice, plus 1D6x1000 credits in cash
or trade items - only the cash is stored as starting money. Warrior-types favour
segmented armor manufactured on Phase World (120 M.D.C.), which can be fitted
with a phase field for an extra cost, and the race favours phase-tech weapons
but can use any equipment available.

## GM Notes

Prometheans become eligible for the second stage at 10th level, on a good
alignment, by passing a Test of Maturity. Helping one pass it is offered by the
book as an adventure or a whole campaign. Second stage prometheans are
explicitly an NPC race - "their power and alien nature make them unfit as player
characters" - and are not importable as a variant of this class.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'first-stage-promethean');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'first-stage-promethean';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-first-stage-promethean-class.sql');
